Find all ordered pairs of positive integers \( (a, b) \) such that the equation
\[ x^4 - 4x^3 + 4x^2 - (a - b)x + 1 = 0 \]
has four real roots forming an arithmetic progression. Compute the sum of all such ordered pairs.\boxed{31}

Determine how many primes $p$ satisfy:
\begin{equation*}
\left\lfloor{\frac{11}{p}}\right\rfloor + \left\lfloor{\frac{11}{p+1}}\right\rfloor + \left\lfloor{\frac{11}{p+2}}\right\rfloor > 5
\end{equation*}

How many ordered pairs of positive integer solutions\(( x , y )\) exist for
\begin{align*}
x + (2y + x)^2 = 131 \text{ and } x + y = 10
\end{align*}

Find the smallest positive integer \( x \) that satisfies the following system of congruences:  
\[
\begin{cases}
x \equiv 2 \pmod{3} \\
x \equiv 3 \pmod{5} \\
x \equiv 1 \pmod{7}
\end{cases}
\]

